WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.100
- So Dallas Mavericks owner, Mark Cuban,

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.430
says that they aren't going to play

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.970
the national anthem before
Mavericks games now,

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.000
sparking outrage amongst
lots of people in Texas.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.650
The NBA immediately
responded and said that,

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.030
as league rules require,

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.740
they have to play the national anthem,

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.750
so that more or less is
not government action.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.530
Now leagues occupy a weird liminal space,

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.061
but, arguably, these
restrictions are probably fine.

00:00:22.061 --> 00:00:24.450
But what isn't fine is that
Texas introduced a bill

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:28.360
to require all sports teams
to play the national anthem.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.650
This is clearly unconstitutional,
it's compelled speech,

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.140
you can't do that under
the First Amendment.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.090
Though there is a wrinkle,

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.090
they're trying to tie
this to public funding.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.530
Now you can't just say anyone
that receives public funding

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.840
must play the national
anthem, but it is possible

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.370
that if you tied it to public funding

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.120
in the sense that if you take this money

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:47.370
then you must play the national
anthem that might work.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.860
It's not clear if this
law is going to pass

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.490
and it should worry anyone
that believes in free speech.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:52.920
But what do I know? I'm just a lawyer.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.953
So subscribe or I'll see you in court.

